A||N||11||DaRkLoRD||Need new daily driver.. opinions?||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||10-28-2001||11:22 PM||||I'm looking to buy a new daily driver to replace my Ford Taurus... I've been seriously considering an early-mid 1990s Pontiac Grand Prix. 3.1L V6, 4dr, automatic. (practical, good on insurance too)<P>I wouldn't be doing too many major mods, as reliability would be the main concern..<BR>intended mods (almost totally asthetic) would be:<BR>hood vents (from a grand prix GT)<BR>tinted windows<BR>aftermarket chrome wheels<BR>*maybe* a K&N intake<P>other than that, it'd be totally stock..<BR>I need your opinions, comments on this car, etc.. thanks!<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||10-28-2001||11:35 PM||||Sounds good.  The 3.1 is just a stroked 2.8, so if you get tired of the GP, you could always swap shortblocks with a Fiero 2.8!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>It should be a good choice for a daily driver, if it's in good shape.  And there's a wealth of info on maintaining the GM 60* V6 here, too!||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||10-28-2001||11:38 PM||||I found another one, a 93 Grand Prix STE, and it has a 3.4L TDC.... sweet. hehe<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000003||Raydar||10-29-2001||12:10 AM||||Grand Prix STE?! Never heard of it. Must be a Canadian thing. AFAIK, the only GP with the 3.4 TDC in the US was the GTP.<BR>They're fast as hell, but the TDC is a fairly high-maintenance engine. You gotta keep "fresh' timing belts on them, and clean oil in the engine, too. If the belt breaks, the valves and pistons will become very intimate.<BR>If it's been well cared for, and you don't mind caring for it as well, it'll probably be a lot of fun. I've heard that you can run hell out of them if you keep them properly maintained. <BR>Anybody else?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||10-29-2001||05:22 AM||||Steve--I don't know anything about the Grand Prix, but the current generation of the Chevy Cavalier is pretty reliable.  Not as good looking as the GP or as much fun to drive, but my wifes' Cav has 55k miles on it (she bought it new) and the only real problem we had was a bad injector about 20k miles ago.  Other than that, it's just been normal maintenance.  It's been a hell of a lot more reliable than any of the Fieros I've had (and I had a nice 70k mile Fiero once).  I've heard that the Z24 package is pretty zippy (especially for a 4 banger).  If nothing else, you can buy them fairly cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||10-29-2001||08:45 AM||||Because I know how you drive, Im going to make several recomendations for the safety of yourself and 78% of the worlds population that you may be able to effect with your driving capabilities.<P>1. Shoes<P>2. Bicycle<P>3. Moped (since you go pretty far everyday)<P>4. Geo Metro 3cyl. auto<P>5. 88 Fiero GT with t-tops and 5 speed (then you have to come drive me around).<P><BR>I bet that grand am STE is a nice car, my friend had a lumina Z34 with that motor and it cooked for such a big car.<P>btw, why do you want a 4 door grand am?  The 2 doors ones look cool IMO (the early boxy body)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||10-29-2001||09:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>Grand Prix STE?! Never heard of it. Must be a Canadian thing. AFAIK, the only GP with the 3.4 TDC in the US was the GTP.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, remember the Pontiac 6000STE?  It was Pontiac's answer to the 3xx series BMW's back in the mid 80's.  With the new body style Grand Prix, they also made an STE version.  It had headlights that went the full width of the front end (center lights were mostly low output for looks - like clear parking lights) and was a 4 door with most of the GT or GTP equipment, but sans all the GT body mods.  The emphasis was on understated refinement and performance.  <P>Not a bad car - and the 3.4DOHC is a sweet engine, but it is higher maintenance - so be warned.  I wouldn't let that turn me off of one, though.  I'd love to find a Grand Prix GTP with the 3.4DOHC (and a 5-speed!) for my daily driver.  As is, I'll stick with my 99 Grand Am.  The 3400SFI is a sweet engine in it's own right.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000007||Fformula88||10-29-2001||10:08 AM||||Grand Prix's are nice.  I almost bought one a number of years back (a 91 I think).  It had good pickup and was all around a pleasant car.<P>With the used car market hurting right now with all of the 0% financing, you may be able to get a really good deal on a GP too.  I dunno much about the 3.4TDC's reliability, but I would recommend looking for a GP with the 3800 in it.  Its just my opinion, but I think it may be GM's best engine.  My friend has a Bonneville with a 3800 SII in it with about 150K miles, and its still running strong and been extremely reliable.  Plus it has great acceleration!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jefrysuko||10-29-2001||10:27 AM||||I have a 92 Grand Prix 4-door 3.1 and it has been in my family since new.  I would rate the reliabitity above average since it is on 164k miles with the original motor and trans.  We have had to replace a few things though.  Starter, instrument package, ECM (twice).  We are only on the third set of tires and brakes and only the second set of shocks so it has been good overall for maintanence.<P>In 92 is when they came out with the lights full across the front.  I think they look nice and you can put brighter bulbs in there which makes it look even better.  The fog lamps even accept 100W bulbs.  I would recomend the car.  I havn't had any problems with rust or any real complaints with the car.  I would stay away from the high performance models though.  You won't get the same mileage out of the 3.4 TDC motor.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Master_Sushi||10-29-2001||12:39 PM||||The 3.4DOHC is a sweet engine, I lust for one in a fiero one day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. You should look for a mid 90's Lumina with one. Yes I think they are a little higher maintenance then a car with a 3800II. But they are much faster. I've been in a few Luminas with the 3.4TDC and an auto trans. They REALLY haul ass, much faster then the 3800 5 speed firebird I sometimes drive.<BR>Grans Am's are a good car. I see so many riced out ones with the mods you listed plus rice ones. They seem to be up in the same level as civics. <BR>If you get a grand prix get the 3800. The 3.1 isn't that great an engine. As other people have said its just basicly the same 2.8 in fieros. A big car with a 3.1 also sounds like a real dog.||||reg||3
Z||000010||Screwie||10-29-2001||01:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B> Actually, remember the Pontiac 6000STE?  It was Pontiac's answer to the 3xx series BMW's back in the mid 80's. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, then I suggest you go with BMW all the way. Probably not smart to say this on such an American forum, but German cars, especially BMW, are the best. Get yourself a fine BMW M3, and you'll never want anything else, EVER!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (Well, except maybe a Fiero as a second car that is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Standard||10-30-2001||03:07 PM||||One of my friends has a '95 lumina with the 3100, that car has some pretty good pickup.  Not fast, but not a slouch either.  Has 140,000 miles on it, too.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
